  chapter: 2
  nextSceneName: TitleScreen-Night
  voiceCues:
  - id: legacy_intro
    heading: A quieting lander
    caption: InSight worked for more than four years, revealing Mars's interior and
      recording its weather.
    audioClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 370238dd324532847932bc089b6881d3, type: 3}
  - id: legacy_retry
    heading: Try another explanation
    caption: Look at how the lander's power changed as dust collected on the solar
      panels.
    audioClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 13306632cdfda074ab31ff2891af448f, type: 3}
  - id: legacy_end
    heading: The final signal
    caption: Dust reduced solar power. NASA received InSight's last signal on December
      15, 2022, and ended the mission December 21.
    audioClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 0a0300a86c54b4a48afeef7514416f35, type: 3}
  - id: legacy_science
    heading: A lasting record
    caption: SEIS detected 1,319 marsquakes. InSight's data continues to help us
      understand rocky planets.
    audioClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: f3ceb6027e1cd2343bed78e0bccc3a90, type: 3}
